From 645fcd9e3eb200a84c73522b443ba24868e80979 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Laine Walker-Avina <lwalkera@ieee.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:36:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] TuyaMCU: add MCU firmware update over the Tuya upgrade
 protocol

Adds tuyaMcu_otaStart, tuyaMcu_otaAbort and tuyaMcu_otaStatus, which
update the TuyaMCU's own firmware with the standard Tuya MCU upgrade
commands: 0x0A (start, image size) and 0x0B (offset + data packets).
The image is read from LittleFS, e.g. after uploading it with
curl --data-binary @mcu.bin http://IP/api/lfs/mcu.bin.

The transfer uses the packet size the MCU asks for (256/512/1024),
waits for each ack, retries a packet up to 3 times, and sends the
standard end marker. It then waits for the MCU's first heartbeat
reply of 0, which shows the MCU restarted. Progress is shown on the
main page and by tuyaMcu_otaStatus. Heartbeats continue during the
update.

Enabled wherever both TuyaMCU and LittleFS are (ENABLE_TUYAMCU_OTA).
Covered by Test_TuyaMCU_OTA: full updates with 256- and 512-byte
packets, a lost ack, a silent MCU, no answer to the start, abort, no
restart, an unsupported packet size, a second start while busy, and
a missing file.
